      'Rome\'s centro storico is compact and largely walkable — the Colosseum, Roman Forum, Trevi Fountain, Pantheon, Piazza Navona, and the Vatican are all within 30-40 minutes on foot of each other.',
      'No car needed for the entire week. Taxis and walking cover the city; fast trains cover day trips.',
      'Italian culture is multigenerationally warm. Children are adored everywhere; grandparents treated with great respect. This destination works for every age in the group.',
      'Evening passeggiata (the ritual evening walk) is a natural group activity — dress up slightly, join the crowds near the Pantheon, eat gelato.',
