    directFlight: true,
    pitch: 'The cleanest, most efficient city-state in the world — where a hawker centre meal costs $4 and the Gardens by the Bay look like a science fiction film set come to life.',
    about: 'Singapore is a city-state of 5.9 million people on an island roughly the size of Chicago, engineered with extraordinary intentionality. The streets are immaculate, the transit system is world-class, the food is outstanding at every price point, and the tropical gardens and architecture are unlike anything else on this list. It is the easiest city in Asia to visit — English is the primary working language, signage is universal, and the infrastructure is designed to be navigated effortlessly.\n\nThe signature experiences — Gardens by the Bay, Marina Bay Sands, Sentosa Island, the hawker centres — all deliver in person. Gardens by the Bay\'s Supertrees are 16-story vertical gardens that look impossible until you\'re standing under them. The hawker centres serve some of the best food in the world at $3-8 per dish. The flight is the longest on this list, but Singapore Airlines makes it better than almost any other airline in the world.',
    gradient: 'linear-gradient(160deg, #0A2E1A 0%, #1A6045 40%, #3A9870 100%)',
    lax: { direct: true, time: '~17h', airlines: 'Singapore Airlines (LAX → SIN)', notes: 'Daily nonstop from LAX to Changi (SIN). Singapore Airlines operates both routes. Longest flight on this list — business class or premium economy strongly recommended if budget allows.' },
    sea: { direct: true, time: '16h 30m', airlines: 'Singapore Airlines (SEA → SIN)', notes: 'Nonstop to Singapore Changi Airport (SIN). Singapore Airlines is consistently rated the world\'s best airline — the flight experience itself is a highlight.' },
